      "content": "okay, i see. that pivot to the \"graphene lattice structure\" makes sense. \n\nbut let's look at the practical side for the pitch. if i ask the investors \"how defensible is our IP status regarding similar existing composites,\" and they ask for a quick summary of our landscape, can i honestly tell them that our patent filing is on a strong track and that there are no major prior art conflicts that would jeopardize our core technology? i don't want to sound like i'm hiding something if they do a deep dive later, but i also can't go in there sounding like we're about to get sued into oblivion. \n\nwould it be a massive stretch to say our IP position is \"secure and robust\" given this patent?",
